{"audio": "1corinthians-12.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 198267, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2400, "text": "1 Corinthians, Chapter Twelve."}, {"start_ms": 2400, "end_ms": 5867, "text": "Now concerning spiritual gifts, brethren, I would not have you ignorant."}, {"start_ms": 5867, "end_ms": 11733, "text": "Ye know that ye were Gentiles, carried away unto these dumb idols, even as ye were led."}, {"start_ms": 11733, "end_ms": 21600, "text": "Wherefore I give you to understand, that no man speaking by the Spirit of God calleth Jesus accursed: and that no man can say that Jesus is the Lord, but by the Holy Ghost."}, {"start_ms": 21600, "end_ms": 25200, "text": "Now there are diversities of gifts, but the same Spirit."}, {"start_ms": 25200, "end_ms": 28533, "text": "And there are differences of administrations, but the same Lord."}, {"start_ms": 28533, "end_ms": 34267, "text": "And there are diversities of operations, but it is the same God which worketh all in all."}, {"start_ms": 34267, "end_ms": 38800, "text": "But the manifestation of the Spirit is given to every man to profit withal."}, {"start_ms": 38800, "end_ms": 57867, "text": "For to one is given by the Spirit the word of wisdom; to another the word of knowledge by the same Spirit; To another faith by the same Spirit; to another the gifts of healing by the same Spirit; To another the working of miracles; to another prophecy; to another discerning of spirits;"}, {"start_ms": 57867, "end_ms": 68800, "text": "to another divers kinds of tongues; to another the interpretation of tongues: But all these worketh that one and the selfsame Spirit, dividing to every man severally as he will."}, {"start_ms": 68800, "end_ms": 77333, "text": "For as the body is one, and hath many members, and all the members of that one body, being many, are one body: so also is Christ."}, {"start_ms": 77333, "end_ms": 88800, "text": "For by one Spirit are we all baptized into one body, whether we be Jews or Gentiles, whether we be bond or free; and have been all made to drink into one Spirit."}, {"start_ms": 88800, "end_ms": 91733, "text": "For the body is not one member, but many."}, {"start_ms": 91733, "end_ms": 98933, "text": "If the foot shall say, Because I am not the hand, I am not of the body; is it therefore not of the body?"}, {"start_ms": 98933, "end_ms": 105867, "text": "And if the ear shall say, Because I am not the eye, I am not of the body; is it therefore not of the body?"}, {"start_ms": 105867, "end_ms": 109067, "text": "If the whole body were an eye, where were the hearing?"}, {"start_ms": 109067, "end_ms": 112000, "text": "If the whole were hearing, where were the smelling?"}, {"start_ms": 112000, "end_ms": 117200, "text": "But now hath God set the members every one of them in the body, as it hath pleased him."}, {"start_ms": 117200, "end_ms": 120800, "text": "And if they were all one member, where were the body?"}, {"start_ms": 120800, "end_ms": 124000, "text": "But now are they many members, yet but one body."}, {"start_ms": 124000, "end_ms": 130933, "text": "And the eye cannot say unto the hand, I have no need of thee: nor again the head to the feet, I have no need of you."}, {"start_ms": 130933, "end_ms": 145733, "text": "Nay, much more those members of the body, which seem to be more feeble, are necessary: And those members of the body, which we think to be less honourable, upon these we bestow more abundant honour; and our uncomely parts have more abundant comeliness."}, {"start_ms": 145733, "end_ms": 159867, "text": "For our comely parts have no need: but God hath tempered the body together, having given more abundant honour to that part which lacked: That there should be no schism in the body; but that the members should have the same care one for another."}, {"start_ms": 159867, "end_ms": 166133, "text": "And whether one member suffer, all the members suffer with it; or one member be honoured, all the members rejoice with it."}, {"start_ms": 166133, "end_ms": 170133, "text": "Now ye are the body of Christ, and members in particular."}, {"start_ms": 170133, "end_ms": 181600, "text": "And God hath set some in the church, first apostles, secondarily prophets, thirdly teachers, after that miracles, then gifts of healings, helps, governments, diversities of tongues."}, {"start_ms": 181600, "end_ms": 183333, "text": "Are all apostles?"}, {"start_ms": 183333, "end_ms": 184667, "text": "are all prophets?"}, {"start_ms": 184667, "end_ms": 185467, "text": "are all teachers?"}, {"start_ms": 185467, "end_ms": 187333, "text": "are all workers of miracles?"}, {"start_ms": 187333, "end_ms": 189200, "text": "Have all the gifts of healing?"}, {"start_ms": 189200, "end_ms": 191067, "text": "do all speak with tongues?"}, {"start_ms": 191067, "end_ms": 192267, "text": "do all interpret?"}, {"start_ms": 192267, "end_ms": 198267, "text": "But covet earnestly the best gifts: and yet shew I unto you a more excellent way."}], "words": [{"t": "1", "s": 0, "e": 908, "si": 0}, {"t": "Corinthians,", "s": 908, "e": 1492, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1573, "e": 1896, "si": 0}, {"t": "Twelve.", "s": 1956, "e": 2380, "si": 0}, {"t": "Now", "s": 2681, "e": 2801, "si": 1}, {"t": "concerning", "s": 2841, "e": 3282, "si": 1}, {"t": "spiritual", "s": 3322, "e": 3783, "si": 1}, {"t": "gifts,", "s": 3823, "e": 4043, "si": 1}, {"t": "brethren,", "s": 4083, "e": 4424, "si": 1}, {"t": "I", "s": 4544, "e": 4564, "si": 1}, {"t": "would", "s": 4584, "e": 4725, "si": 1}, {"t": "not", "s": 4765, "e": 4925, "si": 1}, {"t": "have", "s": 4965, "e": 5146, "si": 1}, {"t": "you", "s": 5166, "e": 5266, "si": 1}, {"t": "ignorant.", "s": 5386, "e": 5767, "si": 1}, {"t": "Ye", "s": 6628, "e": 6708, "si": 2}, {"t": "know", "s": 6788, "e": 6948, "si": 2}, {"t": "that", "s": 7008, "e": 7148, "si": 2}, {"t": "ye", "s": 7208, "e": 7268, "si": 2}, {"t": "were", "s": 7349, "e": 7489, "si": 2}, {"t": "Gentiles,", "s": 7509, "e": 8209, "si": 2}, {"t": "carried", "s": 8430, "e"